Intel(R) OpenCL(TM) Clang

intel-opencl-clang is a thin wrapper around the Clang library. 
It provides an interface to compile OpenCL C kernels into SPIR-V 
intermediate representation, which is then consumed by the 
Intel Graphics Compiler (IGC).

This is a core component of the Intel AI Stack for hardware 
acceleration on Intel GPUs and is required by the Intel Compute Runtime.

Note: This package must be built against the same version of 
LLVM/Clang available in the system.
